      "text": "To solve for \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) in the equation \\(y = ax + b\\) given that the line passes through the points \\((4,5)\\) and \\((8,17)\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Substitute the points into the equation to form a system of equations:**\n\n   For the point \\((4,5)\\):\n   \\[\n   5 = 4a + b\n   \\]\n\n   For the point \\((8,17)\\):\n   \\[\n   17 = 8a + b\n   \\]\n\n2. **Solve the system of equations:**\n\n   We have the following system:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{cases}\n   4a + b = 5 \\quad \\text{(Equation 1)} \\\\\n   8a + b = 17 \\quad \\text{(Equation 2)}\n   \\end{cases}\n   \\]\n\n   To eliminate \\(b\\), subtract Equation 1 from Equation 2:\n   \\[\n   (8a + b) - (4a + b) = 17 - 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   8a + b - 4a - b = 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   4a = 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   a = 3\n   \\]\n\n3. **Substitute \\(a = 3\\) back into Equation 1 to find \\(b\\):**\n\n   \\[\n   4(3) + b = 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   12 + b = 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   b = 5 - 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   b = -7\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate \\(a - b\\):**\n\n   \\[\n   a - b = 3 - (-7)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   a - b = 3 + 7\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   a - b = 10\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
