      "text": "We are given that the line $y = ax + b$ passes through the points $(4,5)$ and $(8,17)$. Substituting these points into the equation of the line, we get:\n\\begin{align*}\n5 &= a(4) + b, \\\\\n17 &= a(8) + b.\n\\end{align*}\nNow we have a system of linear equations:\n\\begin{align*}\n4a + b &= 5, \\\\\n8a + b &= 17.\n\\end{align*}\nSubtracting the first equation from the second, we eliminate $b$ and find:\n\\begin{align*}\n(8a + b) - (4a + b) &= 17 - 5, \\\\\n4a &= 12, \\\\\na &= 3.\n\\end{align*}\nSubstituting $a = 3$ back into the first equation to solve for $b$:\n\\begin{align*}\n4(3) + b &= 5, \\\\\n12 + b &= 5, \\\\\nb &= -7.\n\\end{align*}\nThus, $a - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = \\boxed{10}$. The answer is: 10",
